{
  "id": "ep186",
  "duration": 54.841,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 4.068,
      "text": "That famous beam of light cradling Earth was just camera glare.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Pale Blue Dot from Voyager 1 - PIA23645.tiff",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL-Caltech",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pale_Blue_Dot_from_Voyager_1_-_PIA23645.tiff"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 4.067,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 4.068,
      "end": 11.063,
      "text": "In 1990, NASA's Voyager 1 looked back across roughly 4 billion miles to photograph home.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Voyager.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL-Caltech",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Voyager.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 4.067,
          "end": 11.067,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 11.063,
      "end": 17.933,
      "text": "Astronomer Carl Sagan fought for years to take it, despite officials fearing the Sun would destroy the optics.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Planetary society.jpg",
        "credit": "credit NASA JPL",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Planetary_society.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 11.067,
          "end": 14.5,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 14.5,
          "end": 17.933,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 17.933,
      "end": 27.653,
      "text": "NASA Administrator Richard Truly approved the 60-frame sequence, and the probe fired its cameras one final time before shutting them down forever.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Family portrait (Voyager 1).png",
        "credit": "NASA, Voyager 1",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Family_portrait_(Voyager_1).png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 17.933,
          "end": 27.667,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 27.653,
      "end": 33.373,
      "text": "Most people see a poetic sunbeam miraculously illuminating our lonely blue world.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Family portrait (Voyager 1).png",
        "credit": "NASA, Voyager 1",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Family_portrait_(Voyager_1).png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 27.667,
          "end": 33.367,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 33.373,
      "end": 40.243,
      "text": "In reality, that dramatic ray was merely sunlight bouncing off the spacecraft's own camera sunshade.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Voyager spacecraft structure.png",
        "credit": "Voyager_spacecraft_structure.jpg: NASA\nderivative work: Mirecki (talk)",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Voyager_spacecraft_structure.png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 33.367,
          "end": 36.8,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 36.8,
          "end": 40.233,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 40.243,
      "end": 48.468,
      "text": "Even more humbling, our entire planet does not even fill a dot, taking up only 0.12 of a single pixel.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "PaleBlueDot.jpg",
        "credit": "Unknown author",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PaleBlueDot.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 40.233,
          "end": 48.467,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 48.468,
      "end": 54.491,
      "text": "All of human history was captured as a fraction of a pixel inside an accidental reflection.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Pale Blue Dot from Voyager 1 - PIA23645.tiff",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL-Caltech",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pale_Blue_Dot_from_Voyager_1_-_PIA23645.tiff"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 48.467,
          "end": 54.833,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
